ompleting a process that had begun decades earlier. The foundational event was X, that took place during Holy Week, when a group of nationalists seized key buildings in the capital city, including the General Post Office. The insurrection was crushed within a week and its leaders were executed — but their martyrdom galvanized public support for independence. A war of independence followed, resulting in a treaty that partitioned Y. ID X (8 points) and Y (7 points).", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:42:38Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Ireland", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:42:41Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Easter", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:42:43Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Rising", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:42:44Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Ireland", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:42:59Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Answers: X=Easter Rising of 1916, Y=Ireland", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:44:15Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Ireland became a republic about 9 months earlier than India. The Irish were clear they didn’t want to stay in the Commonwealth. India said we are happy to stay if you change the rules and the British agreed to change the rules.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]